.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_OPEN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_open ,
.Nm elf_open_with_options ,
.Nm elf_open_memory ,
.Nm elf_open_memory_with_options ,
.Nm elf_open_memory_nocopy ,
.Nm elf_close ,
.Nm elf_uses_mmap ,
.Nm elf_is_lazy_parse_enabled
.Nd open and close ELF objects in libelfobj
.Sh LIBRARY
libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open "const char *path" "elfobj_t **out"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open_with_options "const char *path" "uint32_t flags" "elfobj_t **out"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open_memory "const void *buf" "size_t size" "elfobj_t **out"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open_memory_with_options "const void *buf" "size_t size" "uint32_t flags" "elfobj_t **out"
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open_memory_nocopy "const void *buf" "size_t size" "elfobj_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn elf_close "elfobj_t *obj"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_uses_mmap "const elfobj_t *obj"
.Ft int
.Fn elf_is_lazy_parse_enabled "const elfobj_t *obj"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions create read handles for ELF objects from files or in-memory
buffers.
.Pp
.Fn elf_open
parses an ELF file at
.Fa path .
.Fn elf_open_memory
parses ELF bytes from
.Fa buf
and
.Fa size .
.Pp
The
.Fn *_with_options
variants accept open flags:
.Bl -tag -width ELFOBJ_OPEN_LAZY_PARSE
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_NOCOPY
Avoid an internal copy when possible.
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_USE_MMAP
Prefer memory mapping for file-backed input.
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_LAZY_PARSE
Defer expensive decoding until first access.
.El
.Pp
.Fn elf_open_memory_nocopy
is a convenience wrapper for in-memory no-copy parsing.
The caller must keep
.Fa buf
valid for the lifetime of the returned
.Vt elfobj_t .
.Pp
.Fn elf_close
releases all resources associated with the object.
.Pp
.Fn elf_uses_mmap
and
.Fn elf_is_lazy_parse_enabled
report how the object was opened.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The open functions return
.Dv ELF_OK
on success and store the resulting object in
.Fa *out .
On failure, they return an
.Vt elf_err_t
error code and leave
.Fa *out
unmodified.
.Pp
.Fn elf_uses_mmap
and
.Fn elf_is_lazy_parse_enabled
return non-zero when the feature is active, and 0 otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <elfobj.h>

elfobj_t *obj = NULL;
elf_err_t err = elf_open("input.o", &obj);
if (err != ELF_OK) {
    /* handle error */
    return 1;
}

/* inspect object ... */
elf_close(obj);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
Common error codes include:
.Bl -tag -width ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
.It Dv ELF_ERR_IO
File open/read failure.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_FORMAT
Input is not a valid ELF object.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_BOUNDS
Input buffer/offset metadata is inconsistent or out of bounds.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
Requested open mode is unsupported for the source.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_OOM
Allocation failure.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_reloc 3 ,
.Xr elf_section 3 ,
.Xr elf_symbol 3 ,
.Xr elf_validate 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
